{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.QBetaCosResummation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.QBetaCosResummation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Determinant.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.cos_resummation_contracts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.cos_resummation_contracts","kind":"theorem","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-cos-resummation.lean#L410-L424","doc":"The cos-resummation is a **contraction**: the correction factor has\nmodulus at most one, so dressing Form A by it can only shrink `|Q_β^A|`,\nnever inflate it.\n\nA real consequence of the class rather than a restatement of it — it is\nfalse for an arbitrary `M`, and it is the sign-and-magnitude sanity check\nthe superseded `ring`-closed conjunct was standing in for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.q_beta_cos_resummation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.q_beta_cos_resummation","kind":"theorem","line":371,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-cos-resummation.lean#L371-L408","doc":"**Q_β cos-resummation theorem** (conditional on `TransferMatrixEigenphase`).\nGiven the spectral identification, the Markov-trace symmetrization of the\ntwo transfer-matrix eigenphases `±α(q)` gives the cosine of the half\nargument, so the refinement of Form A by half the symmetrized character\nis Form A times `cos α`:\n\n  `Q_β^A · (tr M / 2) = Q_β^A · cos α`,  `α = (z(q) − 1) · h(q) / 2`.\n\n**Convention D.** `α` here is `eigenphase q = (z_D − 1)·h/2`. Under\nconvention C the cosine was *derived* from evenness in `α` (bar\nantisymmetry `eigenphaseC_bar_involution` + cyclicity of `τ_M`); under D\nthat step fails (`eigenphase_not_bar_odd`), so the cosine is the\ndefinition under test, carried by the class, not a consequence.\n\n**This is a genuine implication**, verified by negative control: drop the\ninstance binder and the goal `formA * M.trace * (1/2) = formA * cos α` is\nnot provable — `ring` fails on it, as it must. The superseded statement was\n`∃ x, x = A ∧ x = A`, closed by `ring` with the instance binder unused, and\nsaid nothing about the transfer matrix. Note the implication is genuine\nwhile its *hypothesis* remains circularly dischargeable; see the section\nnote above.\n\n**Numbers (convention D, proton pin, mpmath; witness\n`computations/qbeta/qbeta-cos-resummation-d.witness.json`).** On the\nruled `z_D` base `0.4447004085` MeV (`−431571.8` ppm vs CODATA) the cos\nfactor `0.9991805629` gives `−432037.5` ppm — away from zero, as it must\nbe, since the required factor exceeds 1 while `cos α ≤ 1`. On the retired\nForm A base it gives `+1677.6 → +856.8` ppm. The superseded convention-C\nfigure (`+1677.5 → +305.7` ppm, `5.49×`) is historical. None of these is\na consequence of this theorem, and neither base is selected by residual. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-beta-cos-resummation","label":"prop:q-beta-cos-resummation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-cos-resummation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.cos_resummation_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.cos_resummation_even","kind":"theorem","line":363,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-cos-resummation.lean#L363-L369","doc":"The cosine factor is **even** in `α`: under `α ↦ −α`, the value is\npreserved. (From `cos(−x) = cos x`.) Under convention D this does **not**\nmake the factor bar-invariant, because the bar involution does not send\n`α_D` to `−α_D` (`eigenphase_not_bar_odd`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.symChar_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.symChar_unique","kind":"theorem","line":327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-cos-resummation.lean#L327-L334","doc":"The class pins the character uniquely — the non-vacuity property the\nsuperseded encoding lacked. Two matrices carrying it at the same `q` have\nequal trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.TransferMatrixEigenphase.det_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.TransferMatrixEigenphase.det_eq","kind":"theorem","line":325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-cos-resummation.lean#L325-L325","doc":"Unimodular spectrum: `e^{+iα} · e^{−iα} = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.TransferMatrixEigenphase.trace_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.TransferMatrixEigenphase.trace_eq","kind":"theorem","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-cos-resummation.lean#L323-L323","doc":"The Markov-symmetrised single-wrap character is `2 cos α`. Falsifiable:\nfor a given `q` it pins the trace to one value (`symChar_unique`), so\nunlike the superseded fields it is **not** satisfied by an arbitrary\nsubstitution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.TransferMatrixEigenphase.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.TransferMatrixEigenphase.mk","kind":"ctor","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-cos-resummation.lean#L318-L318","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.TransferMatrixEigenphase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.TransferMatrixEigenphase","kind":"class","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-cos-resummation.lean#L307-L325","doc":"**Spectral identification** (open input, `prop:beta-decay-transfer-matrix`):\nthe Markov-symmetrized single-wrap character of the transfer matrix `M_β`\nfor free-neutron β-decay, on the 2-d irrep `V_{(2,1)}` of `H_3(q)`, equals\n`2 cos α` where `α = (z−1) h / 2` — i.e. `M_β` has spectrum\n`{e^{+iα}, e^{−iα}}` there.\n\n`M` is the transfer matrix restricted to that irrep. The encoding is\n`QOU.QBeta.EigenphaseCarrier`'s §2 `TransferMatrixSpectrum`, adopted rather\nthan reinvented: a `2×2` real matrix has spectrum `{e^{+iα}, e^{−iα}}`\nexactly when `tr = 2 cos α` and `det = 1` (characteristic polynomial\n`t² − 2cos(α)·t + 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.eigenphase_not_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.eigenphase_not_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-cos-resummation.lean#L191-L206","doc":"**`α_D` is not bar-odd**: for every `q > 0`, `q ≠ 1`,\n`α_D(q⁻¹) ≠ −α_D(q)`. This is the convention-D negation of\n`eigenphaseC_bar_involution`, and it is why the Markov-cyclicity derivation\nof the cosine does not transfer to D. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.eigenphase_bar_even_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.eigenphase_bar_even_sum","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-cos-resummation.lean#L181-L189","doc":"**Exact bar-even part of the D eigenphase**:\n`α_D(q⁻¹) + α_D(q) = (q² − 1)² / (2 q²)`. A bar-odd phase would give `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.markovZD_bar_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.markovZD_bar_ne","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-cos-resummation.lean#L164-L179","doc":"**The bar involution does not fix `z_D`**: `z_D(q⁻¹) ≠ z_D(q)` for every\n`q > 0`, `q ≠ 1`. (Equality would force `q⁴ = 1`.) Contrast `markovZC`,\nwhich is bar-even identically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.markovZD_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.markovZD_inv","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-cos-resummation.lean#L153-L162","doc":"`z_D(q⁻¹) = 1/(q³ + q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.eigenphase_bar_involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.eigenphase_bar_involution","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-cos-resummation.lean#L133-L142","doc":"**Legacy name, CONVENTION C — HISTORICAL.** Until 2026-10-10 this name\ncarried the convention-C bar antisymmetry, when `eigenphase` itself was\nconvention C. `eigenphase` is now convention D, for which the statement is\n**false** (`eigenphase_not_bar_odd`), so this name now states the C fact\nabout `eigenphaseC` and is deprecated. It is kept because several library\ndocstrings and probes cite it as the C statement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.eigenphaseC_bar_involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.eigenphaseC_bar_involution","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-cos-resummation.lean#L101-L131","doc":"**CONVENTION C — HISTORICAL.** Bar-involution antisymmetry\n`α_C(q⁻¹) = −α_C(q)`.\n\nReason: `z_C(q⁻¹) = z_C(q)` (palindromic in `√q ↔ 1/√q`) but\n`h(q⁻¹) = −h(q)`. **False under convention D** — see\n`eigenphase_not_bar_odd`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.eigenphaseC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.eigenphaseC","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-cos-resummation.lean#L90-L92","doc":"**CONVENTION C — HISTORICAL.** The convention-C eigenphase\n`α_C = (z_C − 1)·h / 2`, which the block used until 2026-10-10. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.eigenphase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.eigenphase","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-cos-resummation.lean#L83-L88","doc":"**Convention D (canonical).** Single-wrap transfer-matrix eigenphase on the\n2-d irrep `V_{(2,1)}`: `α_D = (z_D − 1)·h / 2`. At the proton pin\n`q₀ ≈ 1.1099785827513808` this is `α_D ≈ −0.0404857773`,\n`cos α_D ≈ 0.9991805629` (mpmath,\n`computations/qbeta/qbeta_cos_resummation_d_probe.py`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.markovZD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.markovZD","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-cos-resummation.lean#L77-L81","doc":"**Convention D (canonical).** Markov parameter `z_D(q) = q³/(q²+1)`.\nMatches `QOU.QBeta.EigenphaseBarMixedD.zD` and the canonical\n`QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.markovZ`; defined locally because this\ncontent-block sibling imports Mathlib only. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.heckeH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.heckeH","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-cos-resummation.lean#L74-L75","doc":"Hecke-Skein quantum-integer differential `h(q) = q - q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.markovZC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.markovZC","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-cos-resummation.lean#L40-L72","doc":"**CONVENTION C — HISTORICAL, not canonical.** Markov-Jones parameter\n`z_C(q) = 1 / (√q + 1/√q)`, kept only so that the convention-C\nbar antisymmetry `eigenphaseC_bar_involution` remains statable. Nothing\nconvention-D in this file uses it; the canonical parameter is `markovZD`.\n\n**Convention C, deliberately, and this file cannot be migrated to D by\nswapping the body** (bean `qou-cxjq`, 2026-08-26).\n\n`markovZC` here is `1/(√q + 1/√q) = √q/(q+1)` — convention C. The\nmigration was attempted and **Lean rejected it**, which turned out to be\nthe right answer rather than a proof-engineering problem: the file's\nbar-antisymmetry result needs `z` to be **bar-even**, and\n\n  z_C(1/q) = z_C(q)   identically,\n  z_D(1/q) = 1/(q³+q) ≠ q³/(q²+1) = z_D(q)   except at q = 1.\n\n`z_D` is neither bar-even nor bar-odd. So `F(1/q) = -F(q)` is **true for\nC and false for D** — a theorem that does not survive the convention\nchange, not a proof that needs repairing. Migrating this file means\nre-deriving what replaces bar-antisymmetry under D, under a distinct\nname; the C statement stays correct **for C** and keeps its name.\n\nConverges independently with `qou-1oxx` (\"the canonical p-n convention\nis not bar-invariant\") and `QOU.QBeta.ZBarParity`, reached from the p-n\nside rather than the Markov parameter.\n\n**The `rfl` agreement with `QBetaSpectralBridge.markovZ` is GONE**, and that\nis the point: that sibling migrated to D in this same tranche, so the two\n`markovZC` definitions now differ. The original docstring's claim that they\n\"agree by `rfl`\" has been removed rather than left to rot — it was true and\nis no longer, which is exactly the kind of stale cross-reference the\nfive-way `markovZC` overload was built out of. ","signatureChunk":0}]}